.TH TIDEMAIL 1 "" "tidemail" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
tidemail \- keyboard-first terminal email client
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tidemail
.br
.B tidemail
.I command
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tidemail
is a terminal email client with multiple accounts, a unified inbox, drafts,
contacts, search, and optional AI tools.
Run without arguments it opens the three-pane client.
With a command it runs headless, using the same accounts, credentials, drafts,
and mail cache as the client.
Mail results go to standard output and diagnostics to standard error.
Output is plain when redirected, and
.B NO_COLOR
disables color.
.PP
This page covers the command line.
Keyboard shortcuts are listed in the client's help (press
.BR ? ).
Full detail is in the project's
.IR docs/cli.md .
.SH COMMANDS
Run
.B tidemail \fIcommand\fB \-\-help
for the options of any command.
.TP
.B send
Validate a message and save it as a draft, or queue it with
.BR \-\-yes .
.TP
.B draft create
Save a draft; it never authorizes delivery.
.TP
.B messages list | search | read
Read the cached mail.
.B list
and
.B search
return metadata;
.B read
returns the cached bodies of one message.
.TP
.B accounts list
List configured accounts (never passwords or tokens).
.TP
.B outbox list | status | process | retry | cancel
Inspect and drive the queue of outgoing mail.
.B process
delivers the due entries and exits, so it can run from cron.
.TP
.B templates list
List canned replies: the built-ins and the files in the templates folder.
.TP
.B skill
.TQ
.B install-skill
Print or install portable agent guidance for Codex, Claude, Pi, or Hermes.
.TP
.B plugin validate | test | scaffold
Developer tools for TideMail plugins.
.TP
.B cli
Open the interactive command menu.
.TP
.B man
Print this manual page.
For example:
.B tidemail man | man \-l \-
.SH SEND OPTIONS
These apply to
.B send
and
.BR "draft create" .
.TP
.BI \-\-account " ID"
Stable account ID or unambiguous account name.
Without it the configured default sender is used.
.TP
.BI \-\-to " LIST"
Comma-separated recipients.
.TP
.BI \-\-cc " LIST"
CC recipients.
.TP
.BI \-\-bcc " LIST"
BCC recipients.
.TP
.BI \-\-subject " TEXT"
Subject.
.TP
.BI \-\-body " TEXT"
Literal body text.
.TP
.BI \-\-file " PATH, " \-\-body\-file " PATH"
Read the body from a file.
.TP
.BI \-\-markdown " PATH"
Read the body as Markdown.
.TP
.BI \-\-template " NAME"
Fill the body from a template; see
.BR TEMPLATES .
Not combinable with the other body options.
Piped standard input is the body when none of these is given.
.TP
.BI \-\-attach " PATH"
Attach a file; may be repeated.
.TP
.B \-\-signature\fR, \fB\-\-no\-signature
Append, or omit, the account signature (on by default).
.TP
.B \-\-yes
Authorize sending this one invocation.
Without it a complete message is saved as a draft.
Approval is never read from piped input.
.TP
.B \-\-send\-now
Skip the configured send delay (still needs authorization).
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Validate and build the message without saving, queueing, or sending.
.TP
.B \-\-preview
Open the editable review wizard on the controlling terminal.
.TP
.B \-\-interactive\fR, \fB\-\-no\-interactive
Force, or suppress, the compose wizard.
.TP
.B \-\-agent
Enforce the configured agent permissions.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print a versioned JSON result.
.SH TEMPLATES
A template is a plain-text file, one per canned reply, in the templates folder
(see
.BR FILES ).
The file name without
.B .md
or
.B .txt
is its name.
A file may begin with a
.B \-\-\-
block containing a
.B subject:
line.
A file named like a built-in replaces it.
.PP
Tags are filled when a template is used:
.TP
.B {first_name}
First word of the display name on the first recipient, or
.I there
if it has none.
.TP
.B {name}
The full display name on the first recipient.
.TP
.B {my_name}
The name of the sending account.
.TP
.B {date}
Today's date.
.PP
Unknown tags are left as written.
.B \-\-subject
overrides a template's subject.
.SH PGP
Signing and encryption are done by the
.B pgp
plugin, which runs your own GnuPG; they are available in the interface only
(\fBAlt+S\fR and \fBAlt+E\fR in compose), not in
.BR "tidemail send" .
Encrypting needs a public key for every recipient (To, Cc and Bcc) in your
GnuPG keyring, and your own key must carry the address you send from.
If a key is missing nothing is sent. Useful commands:
.PP
.RS
.nf
gpg \-\-list\-keys ADDRESS
gpg \-\-locate\-keys ADDRESS
gpg \-\-import FILE.asc
gpg \-\-quick\-add\-uid KEYID "Name <address>"
.fi
.RE
.PP
The passphrase prompt comes from GnuPG's pinentry, which must be graphical.
It is chosen by
.B pinentry\-program
in
.IR ~/.gnupg/gpg\-agent.conf ,
not by TideMail.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The operation failed.
.TP
.B 2
Invalid usage.
.TP
.B 3
Permission denied.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/tidemail/config.toml
Configuration. Passwords, API keys, and tokens are kept in the system keychain,
not here.
.TP
.I ~/.config/tidemail/templates/
Template files.
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tidemail/
The mail cache and database.
.TP
.I ~/Downloads/tidemail-reports/
Plugin reports saved from the client.
.PP
The locations follow
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME
and
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CONFIG_HOME\fR, \fBXDG_DATA_HOME
Base directories for configuration and data.
.TP
.B NO_COLOR
Disable color output.
.TP
.B TIDEMAIL_PLUGINS_DIR
Directory searched for plugins.
.TP
.B TIDEMAIL_IMAGE_PROTOCOL
Choose the terminal image protocol.
.TP
.B TIDEMAIL_DISABLE_KEYRING
Do not use the system keychain.
.TP
.B TIDEMAIL_MS_CLIENT_ID
Microsoft OAuth client ID for device-code sign-in.
.TP
.B TIDEMAIL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID\fR, \fBTIDEMAIL_GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET
Google OAuth client credentials.
.SH EXAMPLES
Save a draft:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tidemail send \-\-to me@example.com \-\-subject Hello \-\-body "Hi"
.fi
.RE
.PP
Send a canned reply, using the Thanks template:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tidemail send \-\-template Thanks \-\-to "Priya <p@example.com>" \-\-yes
.fi
.RE
.PP
Search the cache as JSON:
.PP
.RS
.nf
tidemail messages search invoice \-\-limit 25 \-\-json
.fi
.RE
